From: rtw89-usb-ap-fix <local@patch>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 08:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rtw89: extend RTL8922A TSSI RFK wait for USB AP

RTL8922AU can report "failed to wait RF TSSI" during AP bring-up on
iStoreOS/RPi4. The normal RTL8922A channel RFK path only waits 20 ms for
TSSI, which is too short for this USB device/firmware path and can leave
the AP with poor TX rate selection.

Extend only the normal TSSI wait for RTL8922A over USB. Keep scan TSSI
at its upstream timeout so scan/channel changes do not block for a long
time when the firmware path is genuinely not responding.
---
diff --git a/phy.c b/phy.c
--- a/phy.c
+++ b/phy.c
@@ -4122,6 +4122,15 @@ int rtw89_phy_rfk_tssi_and_wait(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev,
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	if (rtwdev->chip->chip_id == RTL8922A &&
+	    rtwdev->hci.type == RTW89_HCI_TYPE_USB &&
+	    tssi_mode == RTW89_TSSI_NORMAL) {
+		ms = max(ms * 1000, 60000U);
+		rtw89_info(rtwdev,
+			   "extend RF TSSI wait to %u ms for RTL8922A USB mode=%d\n",
+			   ms, tssi_mode);
+	}
+
 	rtw89_phy_rfk_report_prep(rtwdev);
 
 	ret = rtw89_fw_h2c_rf_tssi(rtwdev, phy_idx, chan, tssi_mode);
